--- body ---
## Context
Today's validator errors are formatted as `"filename: msg"`. The
parser knows the line number for every emission but doesn't include
it. Upgrading to `"filename:LINE: msg"` is expected level of service
for a validator; users jump-to-line from their editor.

This was originally bundled in 0117 (parser/validator merge) but the
0117 imagine pass split it out: orthogonal change, doubles test churn
if bundled, can land before/after/independent of the merge.

## Proposed format
- `"filename:LINE: msg"` when a specific line applies (most rules).
- `"filename: msg"` when no specific line applies (e.g., "missing
  --- log --- separator").

## Actions (incremental, one rule at a time)
1. Audit which rules know their line at emission and which don't.
2. Per rule: thread the line number through, update the error format,
   update test fixtures that assert on the error string.
3. End-of-walk rules (missing magic, missing separator) stay
   `"filename: msg"` since they don't pertain to a specific line.

## Dependencies
- Hard dep: ticket 0117 (parser/validator merge). The merge consolidates
  the error-emission sites; doing this upgrade afterward means one
  emission helper to update instead of two.

## Out of scope
- Column numbers (we're line-oriented, no useful column).
- Structured error types — still `[]string`, just more informative.

## Plan (commits)

**C1: Add line counter + mid-walk emissions.**
Change `for _, line := range lines` to `for lineIdx, line := range lines`,
compute `lineNum := lineIdx + 1`. Update the 7 mid-walk emission sites
to use `"%s:%d: msg"` format:
- Rule 3 (unknown headers): erg.go:271,275,279
- Rule 4 (repeated singleton): erg.go:261
- Rule 6 (Closed empty): erg.go:304
- Rule 6 (Closed in log): erg.go:328
- Rule 6 (Closed in body): erg.go:336

**C2: Store header line numbers + end-of-walk emissions.**
Add locals: `titleLine`, `createdLine`, `authorLine`, `closedEmptyLine int`.
Add parallel slices `tagLines`, `blockedByLines []int` alongside the
value slices. Record the line number when each header is first parsed.
Update the 7 end-of-walk emission sites:
- Rule 2 (missing/empty Title/Created/Author): emit with stored line
  number if header was present-but-empty, stay filename-only if missing.
- Rule 5 (invalid Tag value): emit with stored tag line number.
- Rule 7 (bad Created date): emit with stored Created line number.
- Rule 9 (malformed Blocked-by): emit with stored line number.
- Rule 11 (malformed log line): store log-line indices or compute from
  the original lines array.

**C3: Update test fixtures.**
- Go tests use `errsContain(errs, "substring")` — most still work since
  the message text is unchanged; only tests that assert on the full
  prefix `"filename: "` need updating.
- Shell tests (test_validate.sh) use `grep` patterns — update any that
  anchor on `"filename: "` to allow `"filename:N: "`.

**C4: Update helpValidate documentation.**
Add a note about the `filename:LINE: msg` format.

**First test:** after C1, `make test` must pass. The Go tests use
substring matching so most will survive the prefix change.

## Exit criteria
- Every per-rule error includes `:LINE:` when applicable.
- `make test` passes; test fixtures updated to match.
- Documented in `helpValidate` const so users know to expect it.
